# F3 test: directional G38 single-probe commands.
#
# Exercises the four LinuxCNC-style probe variants (G38.2-G38.5) on a
# cartesian machine, in both absolute and relative coordinate modes, with
# explicit feedrates, plus the QUERY_PROBE command. In file-output mode the
# simulated MCU reports the probe trigger at the end of each move, so every
# variant completes successfully.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG probe_g38.cfg

# Home the machine and set a baseline feedrate.
G28
G1 F3000

# Move to a known position.
G1 X50 Y50 Z10

# G38.2: probe toward the workpiece (error on failure).
G38.2 X90 F1500

# G38.3: probe toward the workpiece (no error on failure).
G38.3 Y90 F1500

# G38.4: probe away from the workpiece (error on failure).
G38.4 X40 F1500

# G38.5: probe away from the workpiece (no error on failure).
G38.5 Y40 F1500

# Relative-coordinate probing (G91).
G91
G38.2 X-10 F1500
G90

# Probe state query.
QUERY_PROBE

# Confirm the machine still moves normally after probing.
G1 X20 Y20 Z20 F3000
